  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Version 4.2.0. IPostHandlerAttribute.OnAfterHandle now takes a RequestOutcome (breaking) — the value the handler returned, or the exception it threw — and the dispatcher invokes it on both the success and exception paths. The 4.1.0 opt-in types IPostHandlerOutcomeAware and OutcomeAwarePostHandlerAttribute are removed (folded into IPostHandlerAttribute). Migration: add a RequestOutcome parameter to your OnAfterHandle implementations.",
